		"old-render.ts is the old renderer: peak and peakCols (around its line 220), fullscreen recovery after shrink, and why draw(true) must not run from a resize handler that fires repeatedly (CSI 3J each time). Reference only; hal2's render.ts already has one-way full mode (task cc notes).",
		'The renderer, not app.ts, spots a switch: render.draw compares view.tabs.focused with the tab painted last (undefined -> X at startup is not a switch). frame.build takes `peak` and returns `history` (transcript + pending rows); inbox, notice, tab bar and prompt count as chrome. Peak only knows histories that were painted.',
